snappy opening
first write intrepreter
then Write 5 interpreters


A compiler is best thought of as a pipeline stages. Each stage of the compiler is designed for a specific purpose, doing some work at compile time which would otherwise have to be down at runtime. Between each stage of the pipeline we have an internal representation (IR). We use a different IR at each stage to allow a precise representation of the transforms which have been performed so far. The stage0 IR is the source language AST output by the parser. Each following stage lowers the user program until we reach our target language: x86 ASM at the final stage. Within each stage, all work is perfomed by a single pass. We don't have any stages with iterate to fix point. This makes it easy to be more precise about exactly what is achieved by each stage. The IR for each stage is implemented as a separate type. I have've found attempting to share commonality across IRs makes things more complicated for no gain.

My source language is a statically typed functional programming language (ocaml-like). It has strict execution semantics. It has variant types with pattern matching. Function application and abstraction is curried. We supports simple let-bindings and recursion is explicitly marked. There are built-in types for numbers, characters and strings whereas `unit`, `bool` and `list` are pre-defined variant types.


be explicit about no-goals for a project... for me/barefun
this project not interested to write a type checker. fun, but another day.
don't want to innovate in type systems
dint want to innovate in syntax.
explicit decision to have barefun be a subset of ocaml
precise details of subset to be discovered as I use barefun to write 'real' examples
rules:
every legal barefun is also legal ocaml, with same meaning
(but not every detail of ocaml syntax is accepted as barefun)
if a barefun program is accepted by the ocaml type checker
then the barefun program will have no runtime type errors

in short.
barefun is a statically typed languages, but I was able to cheat
and avoid writing type checker


